From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:41:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 227/342] media kit: BMediaRecorder starts a sound card's node
 as a node too

A producer that is a time source as well (a sound card's multi_audio
node) was only started as a time source, which sends nothing: the node
delivers buffers once it is started as a node. That went unseen where the
card's node is the system's sound output as well, which the media server
starts; a USB microphone's node, input only, recorded nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kits/media/MediaRecorder.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kits/media/MediaRecorder.cpp b/src/kits/media/MediaRecorder.cpp
index b4227875a1..e68ff37407 100644
--- a/src/kits/media/MediaRecorder.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/media/MediaRecorder.cpp
@@ -265,10 +265,13 @@ BMediaRecorder::Start(bool force)
 	// start node here
 	status_t err = B_OK;
 
+	// a sound card's node is a time source as well: as one alone it sends
+	// nothing, so the node is started too (an input that no output shares
+	// the node with, a USB microphone, isn't started by anything else)
 	if ((fOutputNode.kind & B_TIME_SOURCE) != 0)
 		err = BMediaRoster::CurrentRoster()->StartTimeSource(
 			fOutputNode, BTimeSource::RealTime());
-	else
+	if (err == B_OK)
 		err = BMediaRoster::CurrentRoster()->StartNode(
 			fOutputNode, fNode->TimeSource()->Now());
 
